Link gufo_qwen_kernels to gufo_qwen_hip

The SSM launchers in gufo_qwen_kernels (ssm_recurrence.hip,
ssm_row_split.hip) launch BatchedSSMPostNormGateKernel, which is defined
in src/models/qwen/hip/batched_ssm.hip, part of the Qwen extension's
gufo_qwen_hip library. gufo_qwen_hip already links gufo_qwen_kernels,
but the reverse edge is missing, so the cycle between the two static
libraries is only half declared.

Order-insensitive linkers (lld) resolve this anyway. GNU ld.bfd scans
archives left to right and fails with:

  undefined reference to
  `gufo::hip::__device_stub__BatchedSSMPostNormGateKernel(...)'

Declaring the edge lets CMake repeat the static-library cycle on the
link line. TARGET_NAME_IF_EXISTS keeps it a no-op when the Qwen
extension is not built.

This patch was generated by Claude Code.

--- a/src/families/qwen/kernels/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/families/qwen/kernels/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -50,7 +50,11 @@
   ${ROCPRIM_INCLUDE_DIR})
 target_link_libraries(gufo_qwen_kernels PUBLIC
   gufo_core
-  gufo_qwen_hip_common)
+  gufo_qwen_hip_common
+  # The SSM launchers call BatchedSSMPostNormGateKernel, which is defined
+  # in the Qwen extension's HIP library. Order-sensitive linkers such as
+  # ld.bfd need this edge; CMake repeats the static-library cycle.
+  $<TARGET_NAME_IF_EXISTS:gufo_qwen_hip>)
 
 # HIP helpers must share the kernel's wave size, so compile this unit
 # separately while the other Qwen kernels retain wave32.
